Upstream status: https://lists.gnu.org/archive/html/bug-hurd/2026-10/msg00131.html

This fixes seteuids and setgroups unexpectedly changing the current euid/egid.

Fixes guix/guix#10460.

From 9ca6e677dd9b4e307cd175b9a1a86cd700354f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yelninei <yelninei@tutamail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:48:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] hurd: seteuids: Specify MACH_MSG_TYPE_COPY_SEND.

This prevents a EMIG_BAD_ARGUMENTS error.
---
 hurd/seteuids.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hurd/seteuids.c b/hurd/seteuids.c
index 0a1e533bb3..ea93e0c51e 100644
--- a/hurd/seteuids.c
+++ b/hurd/seteuids.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ retry:
     {
       /* Get a new auth port using those IDs.  */
       err = __USEPORT (AUTH,
-		       __auth_makeauth (port, NULL, 0, 0,
+		       __auth_makeauth (port, NULL, MACH_MSG_TYPE_COPY_SEND, 0,
 					new, n,
 					_hurd_id.aux.uids, _hurd_id.aux.nuids,
 					_hurd_id.gen.gids, _hurd_id.gen.ngids,
-- 
2.54.0

